424: en:{
425:   brand_sub:"TWSE ┬╖ TPEx",
426:   nav:{week:"This week",results:"Results",how:"How it works",review:"Review",data:"Data",limits:"Limits",next:"Next steps",docs:"Documents"},
427:   theme:"Toggle light/dark theme",
428:   eyebrow:"Lab opened 9 September 2026 ┬╖ weekly protocol ┬╖ simulation only",
429:   title_html:"Stock forecasting for Taiwan, under a <em>strict clock</em> and an adversarial reviewer",
430:   deck:"Every week, three forecasters pick five stocks out of nearly 2,000 Taiwanese securities. Nothing is actually bought: the lab simulates, archives every step with a real timestamp and measures against chance. This page shows what it has produced so far, limits included.",
431:   st_updated:"Updated", st_week:"Current week", st_weeks:"Weeks simulated", st_weeks_s:"MayΓÇôSeptember 2026",
432:   st_tests:"Automated tests", st_tests_s:"all passing, no network",
433:   st_rounds:"Review rounds", st_rounds_s:n=>`all with a ΓÇ£rejectedΓÇ¥ verdict`, st_universe:"Universe", st_universe_s:"main-board common stocks",
434:   verdict_tag:"Honest reading",
435:   verdict:(v)=>`Over the ${v.w} simulated weeks (MayΓÇôSeptember 2026) no portfolio makes money net of costs in either scenario. Under the standard protocol, Q0 and Q1 ${v.stdBelow?"end below":"do not clearly beat"} the random control (${v.q0s} and ${v.q1s} vs. ${v.a1s} weekly)${v.user?`; with your capital, Q1 ${v.q1AboveUser?"ends slightly above chance":"does not beat chance either"} (${v.q1u} vs. ${v.a1u}), but the confidence interval of the excess includes zero`:""}. With so few weeks and no dividends we can neither claim nor rule out that they carry signal. The lists on this page are the output of an experiment, not recommendations.`,
436:   wk_label:"This week", wk_title:"The week's list",
437:   wk_sub:(wk,cut)=>`Week ${wk}. Cutoff: ${cut} (Taipei time). Simulated entry at the first open after the Monday 08:30 deadline; exit at the last close of the week.`,
438:   wk_banner:(when)=>`This list was archived on ${when} (Taipei time), after Monday's open: it is a reconstruction from data already known, not a prospective forecast. The first prospective list will be the one for the Sunday 13 September cutoff, published before Monday 14's open.`,
439:   wk_banner_tag:"Not prospective",
440:   wk_pending:"Outcome pending: the week has not closed yet.",
441:   wk_scen_note:"The lists change with the scenario: the liquidity rule requires the median 20-session turnover to be at least 20 times the slot notional, so with NT$15,000 per slot small stocks enter that NT$1,000,000 keeps out. The random control is drawn from that universe too.",
442:   wk_universe:(n)=>`${n} eligible stocks`,
443:   fc:{Q0:"Q0 ┬╖ Momentum",Q1:"Q1 ┬╖ Tabular model",A1:"A1 ┬╖ Random control"},
444:   fc_how:{Q0:"the 5 biggest risers over 20 sessions",Q1:"ridge + LightGBM on weekly return ranks",A1:"5 random stocks from the eligible universe"},
445:   entries:"Entries", entries_v:(f,n)=>`${f} of ${n}`, no_lot:"no affordable lot", scen_short:{standard:"standard",user:"your capital"},
446:   no_scenario:"computing",
447:   res_label:"Results", res_title:"Backtest, MayΓÇôSeptember 2026",
448:   res_sub:(u)=>`A week-by-week walk over the ${u} main-board common stocks, using the official per-date quotes and no dividends. Two scenarios: the protocol's standard one and one sized like your capital.`,
449:   scen:{standard:"Standard protocol",user:"Your capital"},
450:   scen_sub:{standard:"NT$5,000,000 ┬╖ 1,000-share lots",user:"NT$75,000 ┬╖ odd lots Θ¢╢Φéí ┬╖ NT$20 min."},
451:   scen_missing:"This scenario is still being computed; the exporter will add it here when it finishes.",
452:   scen_note:{standard:"",user:"Declared approximation: odd-lot executions use regular-session prices, not odd-lot market prices; the 20 bp slippage and the NT$20 minimum commission are assumptions, not measurements."},
453:   kpi_title:(n)=>`${n} weeks traded`,
454:   kpi:{net:"Mean weekly net portfolio return (open ΓåÆ close)",gross:"Mean weekly gross return of the 5 picks",costs:"Mean cost over invested amount",pos:"Weeks with positive net",fail:"Failed entries (of attempted)",eq:"Final equity",tot:"Total return",paired:"Net excess vs. random (A1)"},
455:   ew:(x)=>`Eligible universe, gross and before costs: ${x} weekly on average.`,
456:   paired_v:(m,n,deg)=>deg?`${m} pp ┬╖ ${n} pairable weeks ┬╖ not estimable`:`${m} pp ┬╖ ${n} weeks`,
457:   paired_ci:(lo,hi)=>`95% CI [${lo}, ${hi}]`,
458:   paired_lim:(n)=>`limited variability: ${n} fixed weeks`,
459:   chart_title:"Simulated equity, week by week",
460:   chart_cap:"Value of each portfolio at the week's close, net of illustrative costs. The dotted line is the starting capital. Hollow points are provisional valuations (stale prices or unresolved fractions), not market closes.",
461:   tw_legend:"Taiwan convention: Γû▓ red = up, Γû╝ green = down. The sign always accompanies the colour.",
462:   weeks_title:"Week by week",
463:   weeks_hint:"Click a row to see each forecaster's five picks.",
464:   th:{week:"Week",cutoff:"Cutoff",elig:"Eligible",ew:"Universe gross",net:f=>`${f} net`,gross:"Gross",status:"Status"},
465:   st:{valid:"",pending:"pending",closure:"session without data (10 Jul)",nosel:"no new selection"},
466:   pick_status:{exited:"exited",filled:"bought, exit pending",open:"open position",entry_failed:"entry failed",exit_blocked:"exit blocked",pending:"pending"},
467:   reason:{notional_below_one_lot:"notional < 1 lot",interval_mismatch:"exposure differs from A1",extraordinary_closure_unhandled:"unscheduled closure",missing_interval:"no interval"},
468:   how_label:"Protocol", how_title:"How a week works",
469:   how_sub:"The protocol is the same every week and allows no exceptions. Everything that happens is archived with the system's real time. In a prospective run only what was available before the cutoff counts; the runs on this page are historical reconstructions with data captured after the cutoffs, and are declared as such.",
470:   steps:[
471:     {when:"Sunday 18:00",h:"Cutoff",p:"The information window closes. In a prospective run only what was published and archived before this time enters; in the reconstructions on this page the data were captured on 9ΓÇô10 September 2026, after every cutoff, and the cutoff only filters by session date."},
472:     {when:"Monday 08:30",h:"Deadline",p:"Each forecaster delivers its five-stock list. It is archived with a real timestamp and a content signature."},
473:     {when:"Monday ┬╖ open",h:"Simulated entry",p:"Buy at the opening price, with commission, slippage and the scenario's lot size."},
474:     {when:"Friday ┬╖ close",h:"Simulated exit",p:"Sell at the last close of the week, with sales tax. If there is no session, the exit waits for the next one."},
475:     {when:"Afterwards",h:"Measurement",p:"Each portfolio is paired with the same week's random control and the excess is estimated with block bootstrap."}
476:   ],
477:   fc_title:"Three forecasters, one yardstick",
478:   fc_cards:{Q0:"A rule with no learning: buy the five stocks that rose the most over the last 20 sessions. The simplest possible yardstick.",Q1:"A tabular model (ridge + LightGBM) on weekly return ranks. Trained only on labels already known at the cutoff, retrained every four weeks.",A1:"Five random stocks from the same eligible universe, same seed every run. If a model does not beat chance, there is no signal to defend."},
479:   controls_title:"Controls that make the measurement trustworthy",
480:   controls:[
481:     {b:"Strict clock (point-in-time)",p:"Every datum carries three times: when it became available, when it was first seen and when it was archived. None is ever rewritten. In reconstructions the archive time is later than the cutoff and availability is marked as a conservative inference."},
482:     {b:"Append-only archive",p:"Captures, packets and lists are stored with a content hash in a manifest that only grows. A single altered byte is detected."},
483:     {b:"Verified readmission",p:"In prospective mode, when a packet is reloaded every document is re-derived from the original bytes and anything that does not match is rejected without exposing its content. In historical reconstructions documents are declared unverified unless the extractor registry is supplied; the extractor for multi-capture series is still pending."},
484:     {b:"Explicit costs and real lots",p:"Commission, sales tax, slippage and 1,000-share (or odd) lots are applied with exact arithmetic."},
485:     {b:"Paired random control",p:"The only valid comparison is against a random portfolio from the same week with the same exposure."},
486:     {b:"No real orders",p:"The lab never connects to a broker or handles credentials. It only simulates and archives."}
487:   ],
488:   roles:[
489:     {b:"Brayann Benavides",p:"Author and owner of the lab: design, construction, data, reports and this page."},
490:     {b:"GPT-6 Astra (Codex CLI)",p:"Independent reviewer: tries to break the system in every round."},
491:     {b:"GPT-6 Pro",p:"Starting research plan and protocol (v2.0, 9 Sep 2026)."}
492:   ],
493:   rev_label:"Adversarial review", rev_title:(n)=>`${n} rounds, all with a ΓÇ£rejectedΓÇ¥ verdict`,
494:   rev_sub:"After each block of work, a second model tries to break the system: temporal leaks, tampered packets, forged seals, accounting errors. Every finding receives a fix and a named test, and Astra verifies those fixes in the next round; some verifications remain partial and return to the list. So far every round has ended in ΓÇ£rejectedΓÇ¥: the reviewer only approves when no high or blocking finding is left open, and every round finds new ones.",
495:   rev_chart:"New findings per round, by severity",
496:   rev_cap:(a,b,c)=>`From ${a} findings (${b} blocking) in round 1 to ${c} in the latest, none blocking since round 6.`,
497:   rev_k:{total:"New findings, cumulative",verified:"Verified by Astra in later rounds",first:"Round 1",last:"Latest round",block:"Blocking issued ┬╖ verified"},
498:   sev:{bloqueante:"blocking",alta:"high",media:"medium",baja:"low"},
499:   verdicts:{rechazado:"rejected",aceptado:"accepted"},
500:   new_findings:(n)=>`${n} new findings`, response:"Builder's response", astra_out:"Astra's report", round_word:"Round",
501:   rev_lang:"Astra's summaries are shown in Spanish, as issued.",
502:   data_label:"Data", data_title:"Where everything comes from",
503:   data_sub:"Everything the lab uses is downloaded from official or public sources and archived before use. No purchased data, no private keys.",
504:   facts:(d)=>[
505:     {b:"Official per-date quotes",p:`TWSE (MI_INDEX) and TPEx (dailyQuotes): ${d.tw} and ${d.tp} archived sessions, from ${d.first} to ${d.last}. Phase two (2021ΓÇô2024) is still downloading.`},
506:     {b:"Security master",p:`${d.seg} identity segments (symbol + listing date) and ${d.uni} simulable common stocks, census of ${d.asof}.`},
507:     {b:"Daily capture",p:"Windows scheduled task at 18:30: 37 endpoints from TWSE, TPEx and FinMind, with real ingestion time."},
508:     {b:"What is missing",p:"Historical dividends for the full universe: the per-date source does not carry them and FinMind's free tier allows about 300 requests per hour."}
509:   ],
510:   lim_label:"Limits", lim_title:"Read these before the numbers",
511:   limits:[
512:     {b:"17 weeks are not enough.",p:"No difference between forecasters is statistically distinguishable from zero at this size."},
513:     {b:"No dividends.",p:"MayΓÇôSeptember is dividend season in Taiwan: returns and Q1's labels are biased downwards."},
514:     {b:"Survivor universe.",p:"The current census is used, not the one in force each week; securities delisted since then do not appear."},
515:     {b:"Illustrative costs.",p:"Commission 0.1425% per side, sales tax 0.3%, slippage 10ΓÇô20 bp. The broker's real commission is still missing."},
516:     {b:"Fragile paired excess.",p:"In the standard scenario so few weeks are comparable (failed entries change exposure) that the bootstrap is degenerate and no interval is published. In your-capital scenario the interval exists, but with few weeks and limited variability, and it includes zero."},
517:     {b:"Sizing.",p:"In the standard scenario, NT$1M per slot cannot buy a 1,000-share lot of σÅ░τ⌐ìΘ¢╗ or τ╖»τ⌐Ä; the odd-lot scenario can, but pays the minimum commission."}
518:   ],
519:   next_label:"Next steps", next_title:"What comes next",
520:   next_you:"Decisions that are yours",
